Subject: [PATCH] Enable genuine ML-DSA TLS 1.3 and X.509 verification

Base: BoringSSL 91a66a59b6c1435120ff83e245d7719411294386 after boring-pq.patch,
boringssl.patch, boringssl-loongarch.patch, boringssl-windows.patch, and
agy-clienthello.patch. This patch does not change the cryptographic primitives.

Backport the upstream ML-DSA integration shape: distinct EVP key types for
mldsa44/65/87, TLS 1.3-only CertificateVerify, pure ML-DSA with an empty context,
and RFC 9881 certificate AlgorithmIdentifiers with absent parameters. Enable
ML-DSA in the default EVP decoder set so parsed X.509 issuer keys can actually
verify chains, and retain exact issuer-key/algorithm binding. Default TLS
verification preferences remain unchanged; explicit signature preferences and
the existing ClientHello wire-list API enable the supported schemes.

References:
  https://www.iana.org/assignments/tls-parameters/tls-signaturescheme.csv
  https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-tls-mldsa-06.html
  https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9881.html
  https://github.com/google/boringssl/blob/8f2554dc344d403fd6d628773d39637c323eb801/ssl/ssl_privkey.cc
  https://github.com/google/boringssl/blob/8f2554dc344d403fd6d628773d39637c323eb801/crypto/x509/algorithm.cc
  https://github.com/golang/go/blob/master/src/crypto/tls/auth.go

Native regression coverage: all three parameter sets, mutual TLS 1.3 with
verified ML-DSA certificate chains, corrupted server/client CertificateVerify,
corrupted/truncated/overlong leaf and intermediate certificate signatures,
cryptographically valid signatures under invalid AlgorithmIdentifiers, SPKI
parameter rejection, exact key/scheme binding, and TLS 1.0-1.2 rejection.
The existing wire-only test uses truly unknown groups and signature IDs rather
than IDs now implemented by this patch or the separate hybrid-group patch.

Integration checks (not run by the patch author): native ssl_test filters
SSLTest.MLDSA*:SSLTest.ClientHelloAdvertisementsPreserveValidation; native
crypto_test filters X509Test.MLDSA*:EVPTest.MLDSATestVectors:EVPTest.WycheproofMLDSA*;
then the parent's full native suite and Go/Rust interoperability signature cases.

diff --git a/include/openssl/ssl.h b/include/openssl/ssl.h
index 7816f0c15a2a..40ede7c99b0c 100644
--- a/include/openssl/ssl.h
+++ b/include/openssl/ssl.h
@@ -1146,6 +1146,15 @@
 #define SSL_SIGN_RSA_PSS_RSAE_SHA512 0x0806
 #define SSL_SIGN_ED25519 0x0807
 
+// ML-DSA is supported only in TLS 1.3. These IANA SignatureScheme values use
+// pure ML-DSA with an empty FIPS 204 context, not HashML-DSA. Each scheme
+// requires the corresponding ML-DSA parameter set in the certificate's SPKI.
+// Verification must be enabled with the signature preference APIs; the default
+// verification preferences and configured ClientHello wire order are unchanged.
+#define SSL_SIGN_ML_DSA_44 0x0904
+#define SSL_SIGN_ML_DSA_65 0x0905
+#define SSL_SIGN_ML_DSA_87 0x0906
+
 // SSL_SIGN_RSA_PKCS1_SHA256_LEGACY is a backport of RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 with
 // SHA-256 to TLS 1.3. It is disabled by default and only defined for client
 // certificates.
@@ -1182,7 +1191,8 @@
 OPENSSL_EXPORT int SSL_get_signature_algorithm_key_type(uint16_t sigalg);
 
 // SSL_get_signature_algorithm_digest returns the digest function associated
-// with |sigalg| or |NULL| if |sigalg| has no prehash (Ed25519) or is unknown.
+// with |sigalg| or |NULL| if |sigalg| has no prehash (Ed25519 or ML-DSA) or is
+// unknown.
 OPENSSL_EXPORT const EVP_MD *SSL_get_signature_algorithm_digest(
     uint16_t sigalg);
 
